From 2110a6d1679d149cd556eeb65fb50f4e1a250a8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:20:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend: ASTC textures transcoded for the
 host GPU, output target snapshots

The RTX samples no ASTC (a raw header reads black, no fault). The guest's texture header pools
(SET_TEX_HEADER_POOL, 3D and compute) become shadow pages, mapped with one unmap of the guest range (page by
page, RM's page-table walk ran out of memory); an ASTC header there points at a copy decoded by a worker
thread with Eglantine's own ASTC decoder and compressed with its BCn encoder (BC1 when opaque, else BC3;
EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_ASTC_FORMAT=rgba: A8B8G8R8), re-swizzled to the header's block layout
(SwizzleImageToBuffer, new in texture_cache/util) in a host arena (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_ASTC_MB, 2048).
Only headers Eglantine's texture cache reads (DescriptorTable, new or changed descriptors) are decoded:
decoding the whole pool filled 2 GiB with 29k textures, the sampled ones are ~1800 (1.1 GiB) on MKW's menus.
Until a copy is ready a header stays raw.

EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SNAP takes a trigger file (seconds < 0: when <file>.now appears) and address 0 means
the largest sRGB A8B8G8R8 colour target, now tracked from the 3D front (OnColorTarget: MKW sets its targets
from macros). RM mappings that fail with NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY are retried up to 8 times.

MKW "Start Grand Prix?" screen, host GPU vs Eglantine's own frame: before 15.9 dB, 0.65x brightness (ASTC
black); after 20.7 dB, 1.01x (outside a button Eglantine's frame glitches on), thumbnails, labels and badge
art all present.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
